# API Routes

File-based routing: `src/pages/api/<path>.ts` maps to `/api/<path>`.

## Handler shape

- Export the HTTP verb as a named export typed `APIRoute` (`GET`, `POST`, etc.).
- Match an existing sibling: `@src/pages/api/auth/signin.ts` for form POST flows, `@src/pages/api/auth/callback.ts` for query-param GET flows.

## Supabase

- Create the server client with `createClient(context.request.headers, context.cookies)` from `@/lib/supabase`.
- If `createClient` returns `null`, redirect to the relevant auth page with `?error=` (URL-encoded). Do not throw or return raw 500s.
- Never read `SUPABASE_URL` / `SUPABASE_KEY` outside `@/lib/supabase` or `@astro.config.mjs`.

## Auth flows

- Form POST routes: parse `context.request.formData()`, redirect on success or failure (auth forms use redirects, not JSON).
- OAuth / external redirects: validate `next` with a same-origin path guard like `safeNextPath` in `@src/pages/api/auth/callback.ts` — reject absolute URLs and `//` open redirects.
- Page protection lives in `@src/middleware.ts` (`PROTECTED_ROUTES`); API routes are not auto-protected.

## Adding routes

- Place new handlers under `src/pages/api/<feature>/` using kebab-case URL segments.
- Document new user-facing routes in the README auth/routes table when they ship.
